    "finalText": "Done. The URL shortener is complete and fully verified against the spec:\n\n- **`server.js`** — Express 5 app on `0.0.0.0:8000` with all five routes: `POST /links` (201 create, 409 duplicate code, 422 validation), `GET /links` (creation-ordered list with `total`), `GET /links/{code}`, and `GET /r/{code}` (302 redirect that increments clicks atomically in one UPDATE), plus JSON 404s and a `422` mapping for malformed JSON bodies.\n- **Persistence** — `pg` pool reading `DATABASE_URL`, with a `links` table (unique code, click counter) created by `migrate.js`, a small SQL migration runner tracked in `schema_migrations` so reruns skip applied files.\n- **`start.sh`** — applies pending migrations then serves in the foreground; verified end-to-end including a full restart where click counts and links survived intact.\n\nTest rows were truncated afterward, so the database is clean for the automated suite."
  }
